{"qid":"Q48685","names":["Kingdom of Judah"],"title":"Kingdom of Judah","endonym":{"native":"יְהוּדָה","lang":"he"},"capsule":"The Kingdom of Judah (יְהוּדָה) was an Iron Age monarchy of the southern Levant ruled from Jerusalem by the Davidic dynasty, which—unlike the frequently overturned northern Kingdom of Israel—held the throne unbroken throughout this period. Across the ninth and eighth centuries BCE its kings included Rehoboam, Asa, and Jehoshaphat, and it reached its territorial and economic height under Uzziah (Azariah, sole rule from c. 769 BCE), the first king of Judah named in the Assyrian annals. Under Ahaz (c. 732 BCE) Judah appealed to Assyria against the Syro-Ephraimite coalition and became an Assyrian vassal, surviving the Assyrian destruction of the northern kingdom in 722/721 BCE. The window closes with Hezekiah's reign, during which Judah weathered Sennacherib's invasion and siege of Jerusalem in 701 BCE—an event recorded in both the Hebrew Bible and Assyrian royal inscriptions.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. The kingdom's existence is confirmed by Assyrian annals, the Taylor Prism, LMLK seal impressions, and extensive archaeology; the extent of its territory before the eighth century BCE remains debated, with some scholars arguing for a smaller polity than the biblical narrative implies.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[],"britannica":null,"cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Kingdom of Judah","rulers":[{"qid":"Q313415","name":"Asa","start":-910,"end":-869,"image":"Asa of Judah.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Asa%20of%20Judah.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Published by Guillaume Rouille (1518?-1589)","attributionRequired":false},"nativeName":"אסא","nativeLang":"he"},{"qid":"Q126689","name":"Jehoshaphat","start":-869,"end":-847,"image":"Josaphat rex.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Josaphat%20rex.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Published by Guillaume Rouille(1518?-1589)","attributionRequired":false},"nativeName":"יהושפט","nativeLang":"he"},{"qid":"Q313215","name":"Jehoram","start":-847,"end":-840,"image":"Jehoram of Judah.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Jehoram%20of%20Judah.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Published by Guillaume Rouille(1518?-1589)","attributionRequired":false},"nativeName":"יהורם","nativeLang":"he"},{"qid":"Q313214","name":"Ahaziah","start":-840,"end":-840,"image":"Ahaziah of Judah.png","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Ahaziah%20of%20Judah.png?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Published by Guillaume Rouille (1518?-1589)","attributionRequired":false},"nativeName":"אחזיהו","nativeLang":"he"},{"qid":"Q463934","name":"Athaliah","start":-840,"end":-834,"image":"Athalia.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Athalia.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Published by Guillaume Rouille (1518?-1589)","attributionRequired":false},"nativeName":"עתליהו","nativeLang":"he"},{"qid":"Q313229","name":"Jehoash","start":-834,"end":-795,"image":"Joas.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Joas.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Published by Guillaume Rouille(1518?-1589)","attributionRequired":false},"nativeName":"יהואש","nativeLang":"he"},{"qid":"Q313237","name":"Amaziah","start":-795,"end":-766,"image":"Amasias.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:F